    },
    {
      "t": 371.08,
      "text": "both sides of the equation to get rid",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 372.74,
      "text": "of this negative 2?",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 374.06,
      "text": "Well, if we add 2 to the left",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 376.1,
      "text": "-hand side, these two guys will cancel out.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 379.0,
      "text": "But remember, this is equal to that.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 381.4,
      "text": "If we want the equality still hold, if",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 383.28,
      "text": "we add 2 to the left-hand side,",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 384.44,
      "text": "we also have to do it to the",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 386.56,
      "text": "right-hand side.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 387.8,
      "text": "So what is the new left-hand side",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 389.72,
      "text": "going to be equal to?",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 391.82,
      "text": "So we have 7x, 7x, negative 2 plus",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 395.56,
      "text": "2 is just 0.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 396.96,
      "text": "I could write plus is 0, I could",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 398.22,
      "text": "just write nothing there and I'll just write",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 399.52,
      "text": "nothing.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 400.38,
      "text": "So we get 7x is equal to, now",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 402.42,
      "text": "what's negative 10 plus 2?",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 404.74,
      "text": "And this is a little bit of review",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 405.96,
      "text": "of adding and subtracting negative numbers.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 408.76,
      "text": "Remember, I'll draw the number line here for",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 411.02,
      "text": "you.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 411.56,
      "text": "If I draw the number line, so if",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 414.18,
      "text": "this is 0, this is 1, we could",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 416.44,
      "text": "keep going in the positive direction.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 418.28,
      "text": "Negative 10 is out here, negative 10, negative",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 420.62,
      "text": "9, negative 8, negative 7.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 423.82,
      "text": "There's a bunch of numbers here, you know,",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 426.1,
      "text": "dot, dot, dot.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 426.92,
      "text": "I don't have space to draw them all,",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 428.54,
      "text": "but we're starting at negative 10.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 429.86,
      "text": "And we're adding 2 to it.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 433.44,
      "text": "So we're moving in the positive direction on",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 435.16,
      "text": "the number line.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 435.72,
      "text": "So we're going 1, 2.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 437.78,
      "text": "So it's negative 8.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 439.52,
      "text": "Don't get confused.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 440.54,
      "text": "Don't say, okay, 10 plus 2 is 12.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 442.44,
      "text": "So negative 10 plus 2 is negative 12.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 444.0,
      "text": "No, negative 10 minus 2 would be negative",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 446.66,
      "text": "12 because we're going more negative.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 448.44,
      "text": "Here, we're having a negative number, but we're",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 450.12,
      "text": "going to the right.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 450.92,
      "text": "We're going in the positive direction.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 452.26,
      "text": "So this is negative 8.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 454.88,
      "text": "So we have 7x is equal to negative",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 457.06,
      "text": "8.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 457.36,
      "text": "So now you might be saying, well, how",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 458.96,
      "text": "do I do this type of a problem?",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 462.36,
      "text": "You know, I have a negative number here.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 463.92,
      "text": "You do the exact same way.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 465.82,
      "text": "If we want to just have an x",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 467.52,
      "text": "on the left-hand side, we have to",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 469.3,
      "text": "divide the left-hand side by 7 so",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 471.92,
      "text": "that the 7x divided by 7, just the",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 474.26,
      "text": "7s cancel out, you're left with x.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 476.54,
      "text": "So let's do that.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 477.96,
      "text": "If you divide by 7, those cancel out,",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 479.84,
      "text": "but you can't just do it to the",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 481.18,
      "text": "left-hand side.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 482.12,
      "text": "Anything you do to the left, you have",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 483.1,
      "text": "to do the right in order for the",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 484.72,
      "text": "equality to still hold true.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 486.2,
      "text": "So let's divide the right by 7 as",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 489.54,
      "text": "well.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 490.42,
      "text": "And we are left with just an x.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 493.18,
      "text": "Just an x is equal to negative 8",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 495.74,
      "text": "divided by 7.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 496.74,
      "text": "We can work it out.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 497.54,
      "text": "It'll be some type of a decimal if",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 499.3,
      "text": "you were to use a calculator.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 499.92,
      "text": "Or you could just leave it in fraction",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 501.18,
      "text": "form.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 501.92,
      "text": "Negative 8 divided by 7 is negative 8",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 504.98,
      "text": "-7.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 505.9,
      "text": "Negative 8-7.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 507.52,
      "text": "Or if you want to write it as",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 508.42,
      "text": "a mixed number, x is equal to 7",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 510.82,
      "text": "goes into 8 one time and has a",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 512.74,
      "text": "remainder of 1.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 513.42,
      "text": "So it's negative 1 and 1-7.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    },
    {
      "t": 516.34,
      "text": "Either one would be acceptable.",
      "speaker": "S1"
    }
  ],
